# Auto commit and push

When you finish a task that includes code changes:

1. Commit and push without asking the user for permission.
2. Follow the git safety protocol (no force push to main, no secrets, no amend unless allowed).
3. Use a concise commit message focused on why the change was made.
4. Only skip commit/push if the user explicitly said not to, or there are no changes to commit.
